It’s an evolution in laser vision correction that could be just what your patients need to see their best! Millions of successful SMILE procedures have been performed worldwide and we are excited to be the first in the Northwest to offer this technology to your patients.
SMILE® is an innovative and minimally-invasive type of vision correction using a femtosecond laser. In patient-friendly terms, with SMILE the surgeon uses a laser to create a small contact lens-shaped layer just beneath the surface of the eye.
With SMILE, a lenticule is created inside the intact cornea. The side cut through which the lenticule is removed is between less than 4 mm and up to 6 mm in length, reflecting an approximately 80% smaller incision in the cornea than with a LASIK flap.
Are there different post-op and pre-op considerations between SMILE and LASIK? Pre-operatively, the prep for the procedure is the same.
