As one of the largest processing, sales and distribution centers of stainless steel in China, Wuxi in East China’s Jiangsu province has always been the bellwether of China’s stainless steel industry.
As a bellwether of China’s stainless steel industry, Wuxi in East China’s Jiangsu province has been continuing its expansion of both upstream and downstream industrial chains for more than two decades.
In order to give full play to the application of cutting-edge stainless steel science and technology, build a standard system in line with international standards, as well as effectively help industrial integration, the group standard of the stainless steel industry in Jiangsu province was officially put into pilot implementation on Nov 20.
“What we call the industrial order is built upon the group standard,” said Yang Hanliang, president of the Wuxi Stainless Steel Association. “Wuxi should be the place to launch this standardization because the trading volume of stainless steel in Wuxi makes up 40 percent of the nation’s total.
“After the release of the group standard, we will have a unified standard for the industry,” said Zhang Xuezhu, co-founder of Fansheng Stainless Steel, one of the member corporations of the Wuxi Stainless Steel Association. “I have been engaged in the stainless steel industry for years and now I’m glad to see the industry becoming more normative.”
