The GTC applies to all contracts for the sale of goods concluded between the seller and the buyer, regardless of whether this contract is concluded in writing or orally or by implied act, and for all acts in the process of concluding this contract (buyer's orders, seller's offer). etc.
The seller's offer is binding for the time specified in it or in the pro forma invoice, which is considered an offer. The offer is informative and takes into account the conditions valid on the day of preparation of the calculation and is not binding.
In the event that the buyer is in arrears with payment of any of its obligations or if there is any doubt as to the buyer's solvency, the seller may suspend delivery of the goods until the buyer pays all his overdue obligations, including default interest, or until the buyer gives adequate insurance for its liabilities arising from the purchase price, interest and costs. All annexes to the pro forma invoice - offer (eg sketches, technical drawings, photographs, etc.)
In the event that the buyer has special requirements regarding the quality of products or orders quantities that are larger than usual, the buyer must obtain an appropriate offer from the seller before ordering.
Import duties, transport costs to the agreed place and VAT are included in the final price, unless otherwise specified by the GTC.
The buyer explicitly agrees with this method of repayment and his possible different specification of payments does not affect the order of repayments. In the case of complaints or reclamations, the buyer is not entitled to withhold payments or to set up counterclaims, unless the seller acknowledges them or if they are established by a final court decision.
In all cases, the buyer will cover any increase in transport costs, customs duties, taxes and other public duties due after the conclusion of the contract. The buyer accepts in advance all price increases that occur in the context of partial deliveries or due to higher transport costs or additional costs, or due to a subsequent increase in the customs rate compared to the customs rate provided by the seller in the pro forma invoice.
5. Delivery or acceptance of goods
The seller may also make partial deliveries. Goods are considered delivered when they are at the address specified in the contract and are ready for unloading.
After concluding the contract, the buyer cannot change the agreed place of delivery, unless the seller expressly agrees with the change. In this case, the seller may charge the buyer for any additional costs incurred due to the subsequent change of destination.
Refusal of acceptance on the part of the buyer
The seller does not offer the buyer a guarantee for the sold products, but the buyer is obliged to assert them directly against the manufacturer. The seller undertakes to assist the buyer in communication with the manufacturer and in asserting material or other errors directly to the manufacturer in accordance with the principle of good stewardship.
The goods become the buyer's property only when the seller receives the full purchase price and reimbursement of all costs incurred due to reasons on the part of the buyer or costs that increase the risk of the buyer, in case of delay with statutory default interest and court costs.
The buyer who withdraws from the contract and leaves the seller a withdrawal fee as a result can no longer demand the fulfillment of the contract.
In the event that there is a reason for non-performance of the contract by the seller, the seller is obliged to return to the buyer all the purchase price already received, which is not interest-bearing. The buyer has no other claims or any other claims against him from the seller due to withdrawal from the contract.
The buyer allows the transmitted data to be processed and made available to the official authorities when necessary to fulfill the obligations assumed by the contract.
In the event of disputes arising from the legal relationships to which these GTC relate, the court with territorial jurisdiction is the seat of the seller. The law of the Republic of Slovenia applies.
These GTC can be partially or completely excluded or amended for an individual sales contract only by a written contract between the seller or the buyer, concluded before the conclusion of the contract. If the buyer is a legal entity or an entrepreneur who has its own terms of business, the SPP in question applies to all legal relations between the buyer and the seller.
