Dry ice is ice is carbon dioxide (CO2) in the solid state at a temperature of -79 ° C. It is odorless and tasteless and bacterically static. It sublimes at -78,48 ° C, so it quickly "disappears" under room conditions.
Dry ice or carbon dioxide in the solid state belongs to molecular crystals. Molecular crystals havenmelting points, do not conduct electricity and are brittle.
It is an ideal source of refrigeration for storage and refrigeration during easy transport of food products and frozen dried products. Dry ice can maintain temperatures between -25 ° C and + 10 ° C (eg ice cream permanently freezes on dry ice, refrigeration during transport, wine, grapes, etc.
We supply dry ice making devices from China. The ice has the form of particles from 3 to 16 mm in length, and the production capacity with devices is between 50 and 300 kg per hour.
