Personal data are any data relating to a specific natural person, ie an individual, according to the form in which they are expressed. This is information that can be used to identify you: name, surname, e-mail address, etc.
Where we store your personal information and for how long
Revocation of consent to the processing of personal data does not affect the lawfulness of the processing of personal data concerning you until your revocation and the use of this personal data for statutory purposes.
Right to erasure / oblivion
You may at any time request access to the data collected by the controller about you or the immediate deletion of your personal data.
The right to the portability of your data
At any time, you have the right to request that the personal data we process in relation to you be passed on to another controller.
Any use of your personal data for informational or promotional purposes requires your explicit consent. In the event that you receive informative or commercial promotional content with your consent, you may at any time request in writing to stop using your data for this purpose.
Whenever you have the right to receive confirmation whether personal data about you are being processed and access to personal data concerning you and the following information: purpose of data processing, type of personal data concerning you, users of your personal data, envisaged retention period data source of personal data.
In the event of a threat to the protection of personal data, we will notify the competent authority without undue delay, but no later than 72 hours after learning of the threat to the protection of your personal data.
We undertake to process all collected data only within the listed management purposes or. processing of personal data and in accordance with the Personal Data Protection Act and other relevant sectoral legislation as well as in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 on the protection of individuals with regard to the processing of personal data (GDPR).
