This method works most of the times. All you need to do is, force terminate the program that is using the file.
Force terminating a process shuts down the entire program and you may lose any unsaved data that any other file that relies on the program may have. It is advisable to save all your work progress before proceeding.
In the Task Manager box, if not already there, go to the Processes tab.
From the displayed list of running processes, right-click the one that you know is using the file that you want to delete.
From the context menu, click End Process or End Process Tree. (End process tree is clicked here.)
On the confirmation box that pops up, click the End process tree button from the bottom.
