Damaged partition: Partition damage is becoming increasingly popular now days and the threat arises when creating/deleting the already created partitions. Once a partition is damaged, the partition table also gets affected and it becomes very difficult to retrieve the data stored on that partition.
Part 2 What to do in case of data loss on Mac?
If your data loss is restricted to a specific partition, then stop using that partition immediately. If you keep using that partition, there is a huge possibility that the new data will overwrite the previous one leading to permanent data loss.
