]]> The 1993 Cambodian Constitution states that only persons or legal entities of Khmer nationality have the right to own land. However, this law does not prohibit foreigners from investing in land in Cambodia.
The foreigner can form a landholding company with at least 51% Cambodian shareholders. Again, the foreigner is secured through the shareholder agreement.
On the other hand, if the foreigner does not want to form a company, they can also use a landholding company as the nominee, for which the procedure will be the similar to first method described above.
