In a meeting with garment workers in Kampong Speu Province on 12 December 2018, SamdechTecho Hun Sen said that Cambodia will expand its minimum wage measure to other sectors, including the construction sector to reduce the problem of worker migration.
“But before we start expanding this, we need the ILO to research the size of the market and the conditions, whether it’s the same as the garment sector,” he added.
“In terms of today’s salary for construction workers,for the companies, it is more than minimum … if the minimum is US$5 daily, the company gives 30,000 riel (about US$7.5), because the construction industry is growing fast, and the competition is very high,” he added.
The draft agreement between the Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) and Singaporean firm YHC to build a Logistics Centre in Phnom Penh, has been completed. Both parties are currently reviewing the content before moving to the next stage.
Kep and Kampot Provinces are expected to see more construction coming in the short term, according to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT).
“We already initiated the starting of the master plan for Sihanoukville ,Siem Reap, Takmaoand Kampong Speu” he said, while adding that Kep and Kampot are in the pipeline. “We move to Kep, we are going to do also in Kampot because I believe in a short time you are going to see more construction in the Kep and Kampot area” he added.
“That is very urgent for the government in Cambodia, in particular, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to come up with the master plan for major cities in Cambodia” he said.
